\begin{didyouknow}{Big O Is Older Than Computers}
The symbol $\mathcal{O}$ was introduced by Paul Bachmann in an 1894 book on analytic number theory. Edmund Landau made it famous in his 1909 treatise on the distribution of primes, which is why $\mathcal{O}$ and $o$ are called Landau symbols. Only in 1976 did Donald Knuth standardize $\Omega$ and $\Theta$ for computer science. Asymptotic notation was born in the study of primes.
\end{didyouknow}
% DYK-END

