\begin{beyond}
\textbf{Monotone convergence.} A decreasing sequence that is bounded below converges to a limit, and an increasing sequence that is bounded above converges to a limit. This is a consequence of the completeness of the real numbers and is proved in any course on real analysis; we take it on trust here and again in \cref{sec:asymptotics-newton}.
\end{beyond}

